#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8eb70a-e41b-5bb2-8a1c-c2d892adb8b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{4x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292424} {:answer/id #uuid "782f563b-2517-5b65-b3d1-0639cd3da9d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{2x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a8eb70a-e41b-5bb2-8a1c-c2d892adb8b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{4x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292424} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d39f3ea-9301-57f8-ab08-d613b890416e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2221490e-f21a-588c-b91a-30cee47bc521" :question/math-academy-id "q-347853" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2}=0$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(0)=2.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =2x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{1}{2x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{1}{2(0)+C} \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{2}{4x+1}.\n$$"}]}
